.\" The manual for ~/.local/bin/hax0r. Change it with the help text in that script.
.Dd November 5, 2026
.Dt HAX0R 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm hax0r
.Nd switch every app between the hax0r themes
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar theme
.Nm
.Cm off | on
.Nm
.Cm preview | build | status
.Nm
.Cm clear
.Op Ar option ...
.Nm
.Brq Cm macos | shader | vscode | xcode | chrome | delta | raycast
.Op Cm on | off
.Nm
.Cm raycast install
.Op Ar theme
.Nm
.Cm help
.Op Ar command
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
switches Ghostty, tmux, nvim, fzf, lazygit and Claude Code between the hax0r themes, which are
all built from one file,
.Pa ~/.config/hax0r/palettes.lua .
Each machine can also opt into more: VS Code, macOS's Light/Dark and wallpaper, Xcode, Chrome,
delta, Raycast and Ghostty's CRT shader.
See
.Sx SETTINGS .
.Pp
.Nm Cm off
puts every app back on its own colors for a while, and
.Nm Cm on
brings the theme back.
.Pp
The current theme and the settings are kept per machine in
.Pa ~/.local/state/hax0r ,
so the dotfiles share the themes but not the choices.
.Pp
With no argument,
.Nm
lists the themes and marks the current one.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Nm Ar theme
Switches every app to
.Ar theme ,
along with each setting that's on here.
Run in Ghostty outside tmux, the terminal fades to the new colors over about a quarter of a
second.
Most apps change at once.
fzf changes the next time it starts, lazygit when its terminal gets focus back, Xcode within a
few seconds, Chrome after a restart, and Raycast through its own Switch Theme command.
.It Nm Cm off
Puts Ghostty, tmux, nvim, fzf, lazygit and Claude Code back on their own colors, and turns off
each setting that's on here, the way
.Nm Ar setting Cm off
does.
Claude Code sessions that are already open keep the hax0r colors until they restart.
Chrome, Raycast and Xcode need a step by hand, which
.Cm off
lists.
.It Nm Cm on
After
.Cm off ,
brings back the theme and the settings that were on.
A switch to any theme does too.
.It Nm Cm preview
Shows every theme side by side in the terminal, drawn by nvim from
.Pa palettes.lua .
Nothing changes.
.It Nm Cm build
Rebuilds each app's theme files from
.Pa palettes.lua
and the templates, writing only the files that changed, then switches to the current theme again
so every app picks them up.
nvim needs no build: its colorscheme reads
.Pa palettes.lua
directly.
Afterwards,
.Ic chezmoi re-add
brings the generated files back into the dotfiles.
.It Nm Cm clear Op Ar option ...
Clears the terminal with neoclear in the current theme's text color, passing any options on to
it.
Without neoclear, it's a plain
.Xr clear 1 .
.It Nm Cm status
Shows the current theme and each setting: whether it's on here, what it does, and what would
stop it from turning on.
.It Nm Cm help Op Ar command
Lists the commands, or explains one.
.Nm Ar command Fl \-help
does the same.
.El
.Sh SETTINGS
Each setting is off until turned on, and on or off for this machine only.
With no argument, each prints
.Cm on
or
.Cm off .
.Nm Cm status
shows them all at once.
While
.Nm Cm off
is in effect, a setting's
.Cm on
changes nothing, and its
.Cm off
keeps it from coming back with
.Nm Cm on .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Nm Cm macos Op Cm on | off
Themes also set macOS's Light/Dark, and a wallpaper in the theme's background on every Space
and display.
.Cm on
saves the current Light/Dark and wallpaper, then applies the current theme.
.Cm off
puts back what
.Cm on
saved, including a dynamic wallpaper.
A wallpaper chosen by hand while this is on gets replaced at the next switch.
macOS may ask once to let the terminal control System Events.
The wallpaper is an unofficial workaround: see
.Sx CAVEATS .
.It Nm Cm shader Op Cm on | off
Ghostty draws scanlines and a glow from
.Pa ~/.config/ghostty/shaders/crt.glsl ,
in every theme.
.Cm on
writes
.Pa ~/.local/state/hax0r/ghostty-shader ,
which Ghostty's config includes, and
.Cm off
deletes it.
Both reach open terminals at once.
The strengths are constants at the top of the shader.
.It Nm Cm vscode Op Cm on | off
Themes also switch VS Code's color and file icon themes, which come from the hax0r extension in
.Pa ~/.config/vscode/hax0r-theme .
VS Code changes at once, and its terminals pick up the colors Claude Code's diffs use at their
next prompt.
.Cm on
writes
.Pa ~/.local/state/hax0r/vscode ,
then switches VS Code to the current theme.
.Cm off
deletes it and takes the hax0r theme and icons out of VS Code's settings, so it goes back to its
defaults.
Claude Code keeps the hax0r theme in VS Code's terminals too, since it has one theme for the
whole machine.
Needs VS Code in
.Pa /Applications
and the extension: in VS Code, run Developer: Install Extension from Location\[u2026] and pick its
folder.
.It Nm Cm xcode Op Cm on | off
Themes also switch Xcode, through one saved theme called hax0r that each switch overwrites.
A running Xcode picks it up within a few seconds.
After
.Cm on ,
choose it in Xcode \[u25B8] Settings \[u25B8] Appearance \[u25B8] Choose\[u2026], once while macOS is Light and
once while it's Dark, since Xcode remembers a theme for each.
.Cm off
deletes it, so choose another theme in Xcode first.
Needs Xcode in
.Pa /Applications .
This is an unofficial workaround: see
.Sx CAVEATS .
.It Nm Cm chrome Op Cm on | off
Themes also rewrite a Chrome theme in
.Pa ~/.local/state/hax0r/chrome-theme .
After
.Cm on ,
load it once at chrome://extensions: turn on Developer mode, click Load unpacked, press
Cmd-Shift-G and paste the path.
Chrome can't reload a theme by itself, so it shows the new colors after a restart, or after Load
unpacked again.
.Cm off
deletes the folder; then open chrome://settings/appearance and click Reset to default next to
Theme.
.It Nm Cm delta Op Cm on | off
.Ic git diff ,
.Ic git show ,
.Ic git log -p
and
.Ic git add -p
go through delta, in the theme's colors.
.Cm on
copies the theme's config to
.Pa ~/.local/state/hax0r/delta.gitconfig ,
which git's config includes, and each switch overwrites it, so a switch reaches the next diff.
That file also makes delta git's pager, so
.Cm off
deletes it and git goes back to its own.
Needs delta:
.Ic brew install git-delta .
.It Nm Cm raycast Op Cm on | off
Switches remind you to pick the theme in Raycast.
Raycast has no way for a script to switch its theme, so the themes are installed once and you
pick one with Raycast's Switch Theme.
.Cm on
turns the reminder on without installing anything, say where Raycast's sync brought the themes.
.Cm off
turns it off, leaving the themes installed.
Needs Raycast in
.Pa /Applications ,
and custom themes need Raycast Pro.
.It Nm Cm raycast install Op Ar theme
Opens each theme's install link in turn: confirm each in Raycast, then press Enter for the next.
With
.Ar theme ,
installs just that one, say after changing its palette; Raycast adds a duplicate, so delete the
old copy in Theme Studio.
Installing turns the reminder on.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Where the themes are, in place of
.Pa ~/.config .
.It Ev XDG_STATE_HOME
Where the per-machine state goes, in place of
.Pa ~/.local/state .
.It Ev CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR
Claude Code's folder, in place of
.Pa ~/.claude .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.config/hax0r/palettes.lua
Every theme's colors, and the rules that derive the rest.
Edit this, then run
.Nm Cm build .
.It Pa ~/.config/hax0r/themes
The theme list: name, title, background, text and Light or Dark.
Built by
.Nm Cm build .
.It Pa ~/.local/state/hax0r/theme
The current theme on this machine.
.It Pa ~/.local/state/hax0r/off
There while
.Nm Cm off
is in effect, listing the settings
.Nm Cm on
brings back.
.It Pa ~/.local/state/hax0r/
Also the files Ghostty, tmux, fzf and lazygit read for the current theme, and each setting's
file or folder.
.It Pa ~/.claude/themes/hax0r.json
Claude Code's copy of the current theme.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 0 on success, 1 when something fails, and 2 when a command doesn't exist or gets an
argument it doesn't take.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Switch every app to black on white:
.Dl hax0r black
.Pp
Put every app back on its own colors for a while, then bring hax0r back:
.Dl hax0r off
.Dl hax0r on
.Pp
See which settings are on here:
.Dl hax0r status
.Pp
Turn on Ghostty's CRT shader:
.Dl hax0r shader on
.Pp
After editing
.Pa palettes.lua ,
rebuild and bring the generated files back into the dotfiles:
.Dl hax0r build && chezmoi re-add
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ghostty 1 ,
.Xr git 1 ,
.Xr nvim 1 ,
.Xr tmux 1
.Sh CAVEATS
Two settings depend on files Apple doesn't document, so a macOS or Xcode update could break
them without a warning.
.Cm macos
rewrites macOS's wallpaper store,
.Pa ~/Library/Application Support/com.apple.wallpaper/Store/Index.plist ,
and restarts WallpaperAgent so macOS reads it, because no official route keeps one wallpaper on
every Space.
.Nm
only checks that the file holds the new value, not that macOS used it.
Light/Dark is official.
.Cm xcode
writes a theme in Xcode's own format to
.Pa ~/Library/Developer/Xcode/UserData/FontAndColorThemes .
The comments above
.Fn wallpaper_set
and
.Fn xcode_apply
in the script list the official routes tried.
